      "evidence": "packages/node/src/v3-live.ts:3194-3209. The only production call site derives every argument from the caller-supplied `receipts.issuance` (a `DurableIssuancePruningReceipt` that already records `deletedAuthorSequenceRange`), sets `expectedPrunedThroughAuthorSequence` to the pre-deletion watermark, and then rejects any real deletion: `replay.deletedAuthorSequenceRange !== null` returns `D109D_RECEIPT_MISMATCH`. Because the receipt's watermark already equals `throughAuthorSequence`, every backend takes the idempotent-replay early return (node-issuance-store.ts:809-816, browser-issuance-store.ts:738-744, conformance.ts:384-389) and deletes nothing. The mixed-epoch pending/published capability the slice was built for (the `!authenticatedSettled` skips at node-issuance-store.ts:875/878, browser-issuance-store.ts:799/802, conformance.ts:434/437) is therefore reachable only from tests. Worse, on the one path where the replay *would* delete (a receipt whose deletion did not persist), the deletion commits and the kernel then returns `D109D_RECEIPT_MISMATCH` after the irreversible mutation. The GREEN's own README:24-27 states the design intent has been inverted: it 'replays the authenticated operation only after the existing cleanup receipt path has established ... facts'. Design.md:329-337 and plan-v2:98806-98808 require this method to BE the compare-and-delete after the gates.",
